AN7581: OEM-order bring-up with runtime HIR record selection (009).

build-13/build-15 exhausted the register-layer hypotheses (006
transaction plumbing, 007 clk-en, 008 legacy-mirror PCM clock writes):
every variant still floats the chip-id read to 0xff.  The 10-29
live-machine cross-check (a second, factory-firmware unit, reports
devices/ZN504XG-D/reports/newdevice_slic_crosscheck_20261029.md and
patch009_mapping_and_acceptance_20261029.md) then corrected the model:

  - the OEM non-legacy bring-up never touches the legacy SCU d4/d8/148
    PCM clock registers - on the live machine all three sit at their
    idle defaults while PCM1 runs - so the 008 writes are deleted;
  - the OEM set_gpio_clocksrc step is table-driven by HIR, read at
    runtime from the SoC window OEM GET_HIR uses (0x1faf0000 + 0x64);
    user-space reads of that block return 0xDEADBEEF poison (or hang
    the older kernel), which is why the HIR default can never come
    from userspace forensics - the driver must read it in kernel mode
    exactly like the OEM;
  - ZSI_CFG holds 0x0f030313 on the live machine without any OEM
    write, so the unconditional ZSI_CFG write is dropped on the
    non-legacy path (cfg_write=1 brings it back for A/B);
  - HIR 0xe additionally enables the second ZSI wrapper
    (0x1fbd3010 |= 0x19, OEM SPI_cfg dual-wrapper branch), now
    automatic instead of the 008(b) off-by-default parameter;
  - OEM SPI_Reset pulses SYS_RESET bit17 and bit25 around the SLIC0
    pulse on HIR 0xc/0xe.

Changes (all in en75xx_zsi.c, non-legacy path only):

  - hw_init: read HIR = readl(0x1faf0064) >> 16 via a fresh ioremap,
    log it, and apply the chipScuReg record the OEM table selects:
    HIR 0xa -> 0x1fa20214 RMW (mask 0x1ff3300, set 0x11300|arg1) +
    0x1fa201cc |= 0xc00; HIR 0xc -> same on 0x1fa20214/0x3f3300 +
    0x1fa201d0 |= 0xc00; HIR 0xe -> 0x1fa20218/0x3f3300 +
    0x1fa201d0 |= 0xc00; any other HIR -> no record writes at all,
    matching the OEM gpio_clocksrc_init branch structure.
  - Delete the 008 legacy-mirror PCM clock writes (SCU d4/d8/148) and
    their parameters.
  - Delete the unconditional ZSI_CFG write on the non-legacy path;
    new module parameter cfg_write (default 0) restores it for A/B.
  - 0x1fbd3010 |= 0x19 now runs automatically on HIR 0xe (parameter
    zsi2_en_auto, default 1) instead of the 008(b) address parameter.
  - slic_reset: after the existing SLIC0/bit4 pulses, pulse SYS_RESET
    bit17 and bit25 with the OEM long delays (parameter
    reset_oem_bits, default 1).
  - New parameters: hir_read (default 1), clocksrc_arg1 (default 0,
    set_gpio_clocksrc argument, semantic still unresolved).
  - Probe banner shows the 009 switch state.  The detect relaxation
    (RCN-only gate) already shipped in 005 and is unchanged.

Risks: the HIR window read is kernel-mode like the OEM GET_HIR every
boot, but the first test on the dev unit must still assume a possible
watchdog reset (user-space read of this block hung build-15, H-06);
the reset is recoverable, as before.  SYS_RESET bit25 is the SFC2/PCM
reset - the OEM pulses it anyway; the PCM stack reinitialises after
probe.

Acceptance (build-17, layered gate per
patch009_mapping_and_acceptance_20261029.md):
  P0: dmesg shows "HIR x" then "Le964%c detected (rcn 08 pcn 49)"
      instead of "unexpected chip id ff ff".
  P1: devmem re-snapshot of the HIR-selected clocksrc pair matches the
      live-machine table (0x1fa20214/0x1fa20218 and 0x1fa201d0
      families); ZSI_CFG untouched on non-legacy.
  P2: SWCTRL(0xE7) != 0 after VP-API init, then DEVMODE/CLKSLOTS
      readback and dial tone.

Signed-off-by: ZN504XG-D voice porting project
